  "id": "COMPOUND:21964 - PROTEIN:5913",
  "verbalization": "Cochliomycin A, (rel)- is implicated in targeting multiple pathways that ultimately lead to the TAR DNA-binding protein 43. The evidence suggests that this compound acts as a target for GMP synthase, which is subsequently targeted by Vertilecanin B, and both of these are linked to the TAR DNA-binding protein 43. Additionally, Cochliomycin A, (rel)- is also shown to target Cytochrome c4, which is then targeted by Butyrate, and both of these are also linked to the TAR DNA-binding protein 43. The integration of these pathways indicates that Cochliomycin A, (rel)- may exert its effects through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately modulate the activity of the TAR DNA-binding protein 43. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Cochliomycin A, (rel)- and the TAR DNA-binding protein 43, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
